steps.prompt:
Write an implementation plan for this requirement:
{{input}}

Research the repository first. Store the full plan with bridge_context_set under key {{run}}.plan (overwrite it when revising). Your bridge_post_result is a one-line summary.

Critique of the previous plan to address (empty on the first round):
{{feedback}}

Critique the plan stored under blackboard key {{run}}.plan (read it with bridge_context_get) for this requirement:
{{input}}

Your bridge_post_result MUST start with "SCORE: <0-100>" — 90 or more means the plan is ready to build — followed by the concrete problems, most severe first.

Implement the plan stored under blackboard key {{run}}.plan (read it with bridge_context_get) for this requirement:
{{input}}

Run the project's tests to verify, and report the files you changed and the test output.

Review findings to fix (empty on the first round; fix ONLY these):
{{feedback}}

Review the changes just made for this requirement:
{{input}}

Plan: blackboard key {{run}}.plan. Implementation report:
{{prev.code}}

Read the changed files and run the tests. Your bridge_post_result MUST start with APPROVE or REVISE (DUYỆT or CẦN SỬA also accepted); for REVISE list file:line — problem — fix, most severe first.

Final audit for this requirement:
{{input}}

Plan: blackboard key {{run}}.plan. Implementation report:
{{prev.code}}

Review verdict:
{{prev.review}}

Re-run the tests yourself and check beyond them. Your bridge_post_result MUST start with SHIP or HOLD, followed by a report for the human: what was built, how it was verified, remaining risks.
